WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:07.790
Put a tenant's cheques in the portfolio, each one matched to the invoice it pays.

2
00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:12.830
Cheques keeps every post-dated cheque you hold, until it is collected.

3
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:20.340
You see what is due to deposit this week, what is at the bank and what bounced.

4
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:25.160
A tenant brings their cheques. Choose Receive cheques.

5
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.470
Choose the tenant.

6
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.160
Then the lease, and choose Show.

7
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:44.790
One row for each open invoice: the amounts and due dates are already filled in.

8
00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:48.190
Type each cheque number and its bank.

9
00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:07.500
Choose Put in the portfolio.

10
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:15.670
The cheques are held, each one linked to its invoice. You are reminded when each is due to deposit.
